A parabola is one of the conic sections studied in this unit. Compared with the circle (one fixed point, constant distance), the parabola uses one fixed point and one fixed line. Later the ellipse and hyperbola use two fixed points.
Plan of Section 6.3:
6.3.1 derive the standard equation \(y^{2} = 4ax\);
6.3.2 name its parts (axis, vertex, focal chord, latus rectum, \(t\)-point);
6.3.3 the other three standard forms and a shifted parabola (Example 17);
6.3.4 the condition for a line \(y = mx + c\) to touch \(y^{2} = 4ax\);
6.3.5 the tangent and normal at a point of the parabola.
